The `Tooltip` component uses the `useContext` hook to access the `closeTooltip` function and the `tooltip` state from the context. It then renders a tooltip with a close button if the `tooltip` state is truthy.

The `Button` component uses the `useContext` hook to access the `openTooltip` function and then calls it when the button is clicked, passing the tooltip text as an argument.

Finally, in the `App` component, we wrap the entire app with the `TooltipProvider` component and render two buttons with tooltips. The `Tooltip` component is also rendered, but it will only display a tooltip if one is open. When a button is clicked, the tooltip will be displayed and the close button will be visible. When the close button is clicked, the tooltip will be closed. If another button is clicked while a tooltip is still open, the previous tooltip will be closed and the new one will be displayed.

